  "summary_en": "US federal regulation (49 CFR Part 395) setting hours-of-service limits for commercial motor vehicle drivers, exemptions, records of duty status, and electronic logging device (ELD) requirements and technical specifications. It concerns human drivers and fatigue-related safety, with no AI or autonomous-system provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Property-carrying drivers: 11 hours driving within a 14-hour window after 10 hours off duty; 30-minute break after 8 hours driving.",
   "Weekly limits of 60/70 hours on duty in 7/8 days, with 34-hour restart.",
   "Motor carriers must use registered ELDs to record duty status, with driver certification and data retention.",
   "Numerous exemptions (short-haul, agricultural, oilfield, utility, adverse conditions).",
   "Appendix A sets ELD functional specifications, registration, certification and data-transfer standards."
  ],
